# Angular & SCSS Coding Standards (2026)

## Language & Technology Constraints
- Always write component styles using SCSS. Never use vanilla CSS.
- Component architecture MUST use Angular Standalone Components.

## SCSS Architectural Rules
- ALWAYS wrap the entire style sheet inside the `:host` selector to enforce strict View Encapsulation. Use `:host-context` only when styling depends on external classes.
- Use advanced SCSS nesting (maximum 3 levels deep to avoid over-specificity).
- Leverage modern Sass module syntax: ALWAYS use `@use` for imports, NEVER use the deprecated `@import`.
- Extract repetitive layout patterns (e.g., flex center, anti-gravity animations) into SCSS mixins.
- Maintain a local color/spacing variable palette using SCSS variables at the top of the file, or reference Global Material Design tokens via `@use '@angular/material' as mat;`.

## Component Integration & Safety
- NEVER use `::ng-deep` globally. If overriding Angular Material styles is mandatory, it MUST be strictly nested inside `:host ::ng-deep` to prevent style bleeding.
- Ensure the component's `.ts` file correctly links to the stylesheet via `styleUrl: './component.scss'` (singular string, not arrays, matching Angular modern standards).
- Optimize SCSS output by utilizing the parent selector reference `&` for pseudo-classes (`&:hover`, `&:focus`) and BEM modifiers if applicable.

